<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions bonds worth 50 million rupees.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions bonds worth 50 million rupees.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Tuesday it had auctioned six-month Short Term Federal Bonds worth 50 million rupees at an average yield of 13.4995 percent.</p>
<p>The bank received bids for 1.4 billion rupees out of which bids for 50 million were accepted.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
